# 25 -- graded failures: FAILSCORE_GRADING ON with a PC_FAILPROBE probe.
#
# Example 02's seeded random search, with a lattice-constant window on the
# cohesive-energy script: --hotvar hot_a0 3.25 3.33 accepts a relaxed bcc
# lattice of 3.25-3.33 A around Ta's 3.30 A. A candidate that relaxes
# outside it fails. With FAILSCORE_GRADING ON such a failure is not the
# constant FAILSCORE but a graded value in [0.999*FAILSCORE, FAILSCORE)
# that falls as the lattice approaches the window (band A); feasible
# candidates are unaffected. Six of the 60 candidates fail this way here:
# hpo_run.log counts them ("Graded failures : 6", "A=6"); its per-eval
# "rejecting (hot_a0=...)" warnings are rate-limited and show five.
#
# PC_FAILPROBE runs ../common/lammps/failprobe.in (the probe from the
# documentation) at the front of every evaluation: a minimiser-free
# sanity scalar S (0 for a sane potential; outvar.tadah column S). It
# grades the failures that cannot measure themselves -- a run killed at
# its deadline, a crashed potential build (bands C and D) -- which this
# well-behaved box never produces. No --gate: set one only after
# calibrating S on your seed.

OPTIMIZER
  STRATEGY
    TYPE PLAIN
    LIB TADAH
    ALGO RANDOM
    MAXEVAL 60
    SEED 1234
  ENDSTRATEGY
ENDOPTIMIZER

LOSS L2
FAILSCORE 1e9
FAILSCORE_GRADING ON
PC_ERMSE 0 0.0001
PC_FAILPROBE --script ../common/lammps/failprobe.in --outvar S --s0 0.5
PC_LAMMPS --script ../common/lammps/Ecoh.in --hotvar hot_a0 3.25 3.33 3.302 --varloss Ecoh 8.10 800

OPTIM RCUT2B  (1) 4.0 6.0
OPTIM SGRIDMB (1) 0.1 0.4

OUTPUT 1
BOUTPUT 1
